---
import Article from "../layouts/Article.astro";
---

<Article title="Animatronic Billy" kicker="NCSU FEDD" kickerHref="/projects">
    <p class="prose dropcap">
        As part of NC State's First-Year Engineering Design Development (FEDD) program, I worked in a group of five to build a life-sized animatronic replica of Billy the Puppet from the <em>Saw</em> franchise. My contributions focused on circuit design and programming: wiring the servo motor controls, integrating sensors, and writing the firmware that drove Billy's movements. The result was a fully functional animatronic capable of synchronized eye and jaw movements.
    </p>

    <figure>
        <video controls preload="metadata" playsinline>
            <source src="/FEDD1.mov" type="video/quicktime" />
            <source src="/FEDD1.mov" type="video/mp4" />
            Your browser does not support the video tag.
        </video>
    </figure>

    <figure>
        <img src="/img/fedd-2.jpg" width="1600" height="1200" alt="FEDD project photo 1" loading="lazy" />
    </figure>

    <figure>
        <img src="/img/fedd-3.jpg" width="1600" height="1200" alt="FEDD project photo 2" loading="lazy" />
    </figure>
</Article>

